# L §5.11 as if: "A pin whose key is a hole, a law, known or wording pin whose date is a hole, and an ask's law or as
# known that is a hole make the value inside the as if, or the ask line, a hole carrying their questions, and nothing
# inside is evaluated". lawd, kd and kh have no rows (HOLE-UNGOVERNED, L §4.6 step 5: read with no law date, "x: no
# value"). (Was REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED §5.11 and §5.18: pins and an ask law that are holes.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
index ks = [ka, kb]
input lawd: date
input kd: date
input kh: key ks
input r[k in ks]: int
input x: int
def f: int = x + 1 at reader

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  r[ka] = 1 "s"
  r[kb] = 2 "s"
  x = 1 "s"

ask q1: f with law lawd
ask q2: f with known kd law 2026-06-30
ask q3: r[ka] with r[kh] = 5 law 2026-06-30
ask q4: (f as if {law lawd}) + 1 law 2026-06-30
ask q5: x law lawd
ask q6: x as known kd
=== expect
q1: ?"lawd: no value" (lawd)
q2: ?"kd: no value at 2026-06-30" (kd)
q3: ?"kh: no value at 2026-06-30" (kh)
q4: ?"lawd: no value at 2026-06-30" (lawd)
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
q5: ?"lawd: no value" (lawd)
q6: ?"kd: no value" (kd)
